          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} Moduli spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            and of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            for a complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+group"} algebraic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            have been widely studied in geometry, with many deep results, especially for the case that the base space is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curve"} complex curve
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            presented in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA+explained"} FGA explained
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            with certain parameters fixed, so called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quot+schemes"} Quot schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+bundles"} stable bundles
            on a Riemann surface, which is deeply relevant for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan%E2%80%93Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan–Seshadri theorem
            relates it to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
            (and to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} self-dual solutions of Yang-Mills equations
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+Lie+algebras"} affine Lie algebras
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+groups"} loop groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+systems"} Hitchin systems
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#OverCurvesAndTheLanglandsCorrespondence Bundles over curves and the Langlands correspondence
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Lie+group"} complex Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curve"} complex curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            (which are equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            when
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi n
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \coprod_{n} GL(n,\mathbb{C})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+coset+space"} double coset space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"} quotient stack
            of the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            around finitely many points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            – the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+uniformization+theorem"} Weil uniformization theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OverRealSurfaces"} Over smooth real surfaces
          %p and then we discuss the complex-analytic version
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OverComplexCurves"} Over complex curves
          %p
            Notice here that the sub-moduli space of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundles"} stable
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
            to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            and via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            relation of that to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            an ingredient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            etc. This relation serves to explain to some extent why this object is of such interest.
          %p
            Now the double quotient description is noteworthy because in this incarnation the moduli stack has, via the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            and in fact in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            over any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
          %ul
